</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-09-04.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="213025"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#213025" label="[21:30:25]">&lt;jleightcap&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: that's interesting to hear.</span></div><div class="line" id="213108"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#213108" label="[21:31:08]">&lt;jleightcap&gt;</a></span><span class="message">i've shifted my focus to implementing a stack machine, after looking into knight's ISA it's too complex for TTL</span></div><div class="line" id="213825"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#213825" label="[21:38:25]">&lt;jleightcap&gt;</a></span><span class="message">happy to report back to this channel my progress!</span></div><div class="line" id="233141"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#233141" label="[23:31:41]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">jleightcap: nice; I am guessing something probably along the lines of <a rel="nofollow" href="https://users.ece.cmu.edu/~koopman/stack_computers/sec4_2.html">https://users.ece.cmu.edu/~koopman/stack_computers/sec4_2.html</a>  ?</span></div><div class="line" id="233220"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#233220" label="[23:32:20]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">or hardcoded instructions?</span></div><div class="line" id="233416"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#233416" label="[23:34:16]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(the only recommendation I have is include signed and unsigned 32bit operations and a handful of byte instructions and you'll be able to get to M2-Planet+unxz)</span></div><div class="line" id="235829"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#235829" label="[23:58:29]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">JMP.Z IMMEDIATE, NOT, AND, OR and XOR would in theory be enough to be turing complete but BRANCH, RETURN, push immediate and add/sub logic would greatly simplify early programming steps.</span></div><br /></div></body></html>